WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.265
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will automate a repeatable task

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:10.530
with visible outcomes. Manual copying between systems costs time and hides failures when

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.795
there is no recorded execution history. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:19.440
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.993
A workflow posts new calls to a team channel, and a custom field

00:00:24.993 --> 00:00:29.947
records the fire district on each call. Automate repeated administrative steps and connect

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:34.900
Resgrid to the other systems you use. The examples in this series use

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.710
a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:45.085
Workflows. Automations triggered by department events. Start with one workflow for a task

00:00:45.085 --> 00:00:47.750
you repeat, and review its runs.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:54.315
User-defined fields. Custom fields on calls, personnel and other records. Add only the

00:00:54.315 --> 00:00:56.150
fields you must capture.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:02.647
API and MCP integrations. API and MCP access for other systems. Create credentials

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:06.730
for each integration and limit what they can access.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:13.358
New Workflow. Create an automation workflow. Have the destination systems and credentials ready,

00:01:13.358 --> 00:01:16.140
and decide who owns each automation.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:22.809
Workflow Runs. The history of workflow runs, including failures. Have the destination systems

00:01:22.809 --> 00:01:27.010
and credentials ready, and decide who owns each automation.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:33.075
Import and migration planning. Plan moving your data from another system into Resgrid.

00:01:33.075 --> 00:01:38.540
Have the destination systems and credentials ready, and decide who owns each automation.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.688
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Choose one event

00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:50.235
and an approved destination for a workflow. Step 2. Configure the workflow action,

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:55.783
data mapping, and integration access. Step 3. Trigger a controlled demo event and

00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:58.770
review Workflow Runs for success or failure.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:04.804
Now verify the result. Confirm the intended action at the destination and inspect

00:02:04.804 --> 00:02:10.238
the recorded run. Test a controlled failure and document who owns retries. A

00:02:10.238 --> 00:02:15.672
common problem to watch for: A saved workflow is not evidence that its

00:02:15.672 --> 00:02:20.270
destination received data. Protected content requires the separately reviewed egress path.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.306
Your practice task is simple. Create a demo-only new-call workflow and inspect its

00:02:26.306 --> 00:02:31.741
run. Record successful and failed execution evidence, owner, and recovery steps. Record the

00:02:31.741 --> 00:02:37.177
result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the

00:02:37.177 --> 00:02:40.940
linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

